                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "So there are pro's and cons for this tool. I will cover both and people should be able to tell if they should actually spend the time learning the tool.\n\nPros\n- The layout and UI of the tool is actually very good. Within about 3 min you know where everything is\n- This single tool will allow you to add new weapons, new armor and new models to the game\n- Easy to upload and create an entry to workshop with little to no effort\n- Supports fairly common 3d model file types of for .fxb\n- Models only require a single bone where the handle is\n- Essentially can create anything and upload as long as you have the know how\n\nCons\n- This tool requires one to have prior knowledge of 3d modeling and texturing to make anything\n- NO ACCESS TO GAME ASSETS!! (This means you can not create or modify current in game items nor can you use the \n   models already in the game to quickly create a new item/armor)\n- Stat locks to prevent \"Overpowered\" items. In turn all items created are quite weaker then the top weapons already in the game.\n\nThis is the first implementation of the mod tool. Meaning later tools and or updates to this tool will be more expansive hopefully. As the tool is now it is not a tool I would suggest to 90% of the people who are interested in it. This is purely for people who already have knowledge and ability for modeling and modding. If you are however a modeler then this tool is great and very easy to use. \n\nPS: The biggest recomendation I could make is to add access to game assets so people can \"piggyback\" models already in game to create new weapons and armor easily.",
